{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The words of Agur:</b> He lived in the days of Solomon, walking in his uprightness, possessing knowledge, and honored in his generation; therefore King Solomon gathered the words of his wisdom into his book." "<b>Bin</b> — with a ḥirik, like בצרי, like ריש and רש, בן נון, בן לילה, בן הכות." "<b>Ha-massa:</b> The prophecy, as in the matter of 'HaShem bearing (נושא) a burden for a man.'" "<b>Ne'um</b> — on the pattern of זבול." "<b>Ha-gever:</b> That is, Agur, in the sense that his wisdom had grown strong." "<b>Ithiel and Ukal:</b> They were sages, colleagues of Agur, or his disciples." "<b>Another interpretation:</b> 'Ben Yaqeh' — בן יקהת עמים. For it was on account of David that the following were said to his son: 'Solomon,' 'Ben Yaqeh,' and 'Qohelet,' and 'Agur' — it is the speech of the gevir to Ithiel regarding the matter of the women and the horses. For he said: 'I will multiply' — and 'I did not restrain my heart,' and 'Ukal' — 'for I was a fool.' Afterward Ithiel takes comfort and says: 'I have acted like one who has not learned wisdom, and does not possess the knowledge of the holy ones.' And Qohelet sought to know through judgment to acquit and to convict without witnesses, but the Torah spoke only by the mouth of witnesses. And concerning this it is said: 'Qohelet sought,' etc. — that he be answered from the heavens, but it was not so for him. Or he said and wrote: 'Upright words of truth,' on behalf of the Torah: 'Every word of Elohim is refined; do not add,' etc. 'And I did not ask' — I should have asked; I asked what I had no business asking. How was it with Moses, who ascended to heaven and descended, and Aaron, who gathered spirit, as it is said, 'and he stood between the living and the dead,' and Elijah, who wrapped water in his mantle, and Joshua, who made the sun stand still over the entire earth — 'Sun, in Gibeon, be still' (דום)?!"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {6 "The text is difficult throughout: identities shift between first and third person, the logic of each proposed reading is compressed nearly to obscurity, and several phrases resist clear parsing. Translated hyper-literally without smoothing. The phrase 'או אמר וכתוב' may be corrupt or elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:51.294849230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}